        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115-a1-a2">

                <pb facs="0353" n="295" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg295"/>


                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tlacotalpam,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 20, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir and Friend:</hi> * * * * * *</p>
                <p>It gives me much pleasure to learn, from your letter of the 22d June, that Santa
                    Anna had failed in his secret intentions against this country. I have since
                    received copies of the correspondence between the government, you, and him, by
                    way of Vera Cruz, and had it published immediately.</p>
                <p>Things have changed here wonderfully. We have reconquered this city, thanks to
                    the valor and patriotism of the loyal Mexicans who are with me to make war on
                    the enemy on this coast, as you will see by the correspondence I send you for
                    transmission to the government, which I hope you will do after you read it.</p>
                <p>The enemy has no place of refuge in this part of the country now but Alvarado,
                    which is only kept by the gunboats; but the garrison is small, and it dreads an
                    attack from us; and this we will do as soon as the health of our men permits, if
                    the enemy does not evacuate the place soon, which it is said he will do very
                    soon.</p>
                <p>Your very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ALEJANDRO GARCIA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Minister Señor Don <hi rendition="#small-caps">Matias Romero</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
